  "feature1": {
    "prompt": "The xr.where(..., keep_attrs=True) function currently overwrites coordinate attributes by replacing them with variable attributes, which is not the intended behavior. In the reported issue, coordinate attributes (for example, those of the 'time' coordinate) are lost instead of being preserved as expected. This problem has been observed since version 2022.06.0 and indicates that the core logic for attribute propagation in the where function is flawed. The fix should ensure that when keep_attrs is enabled, the attributes coming from the x parameter \u2013 including global attributes, data variable attributes, and especially coordinate attributes \u2013 are correctly copied over to the result.",
    "hint_texts": "This feature involves modifying the core logic in xarray/core/computation.py. You need to update the where function so that after calling apply_ufunc, the function rebuilds the attributes from x and assigns them to the result. Make sure to handle global attributes, attributes on data variables, and iterate over result.coords to correctly copy coordinate-specific attributes. Also, pay attention to the special case where x may not be a Dataset while y is, requiring conditional logic to assign the attributes appropriately.",
    "entrypoint": "File: xarray/core/computation.py; Function: where. Focus on the code block starting right after the call to apply_ufunc (around lines 1855\u20131875 in the diff) where the attributes are rebuilt. Ensure that both global attributes and individual variable/coordinate attributes from x are assigned to the result, handling any special cases (such as when x is promoted to a Dataset).",
